  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> hypo solution is used for the titration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of copper sulphate solution, in the presence of excess of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KI</mi></math> using starch as an indicator. The molarity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;(nearest integer)</p><p>Given :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#8212;</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>6</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></math></p>",
